In steady policy, amid mixed inflation signals from tariffs and oil.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:26.780
Earning season continues with guidance revisions drawing attention in retail and technology

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:27.640
hardware names.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.000
Raised sales guidance can shift a stock's investment case when its signals sustained demand

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.660
rather than one-time factors.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:40.080
Dollar-Rama's recent upward revision in sales outlook shows how Canadian retailers are

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.520
navigating higher input costs while still expanding same-store sales.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:50.780
Investors can screen for similar names on platforms like WealthSimple or QuestRade by filtering

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:56.220
TSX listed consumer stocks for positive guidance changes in the last quarter, combined

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.960
with free cash flow growth above 10%.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:03.940
This approach worked well in the mid-2000s when consumer staples held up during rate

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.960
hikes because volume growth offset margin pressure.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.580
The risk lies in overpaying after the initial move, so pair the screen with a check that

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.920
the stock trades below its 52-week high by at least 15%.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:22.800
Canadian investors can hold these in a TFSA to avoid dividend withholding taxes that would

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.540
otherwise reduce compounding.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:29.640
Always verify the guidance language in the earnings release itself rather than relying

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:30.440
on headlines.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:37.280
Imagine you bought a high-growth Canadian stock last month inside your TFSA at $28 per

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:40.220
share, and it has already climbed to $35.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:46.340
dollars. The mechanism that matters here is that all gains stay completely tax-free, unlike

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:50.780
a non-registered account where you would owe tax on the capital gain at your marginal

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:56.880
rate. What most retail investors do not realize is that US dividend-paying stocks inside

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:03.940
a TFSA still face 15% withholding tax on dividends, so it often makes sense to hold Canadian

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:09.580
dividend payers or growth names instead. The pro tip is to track your contribution room

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:16.400
annually through the CRA My Account Portal and avoid over-contributing, which triggers a 1% per

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:22.980
month penalty on the excess. High growth assets belong in the TFSA because the tax-free compounding

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:28.180
effect is largest on names that can deliver 20% or higher annual returns over time.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.500
The concrete misconception to avoid is treating the TFSA like a high interest savings account,

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.100
rather than a long-term compounding vehicle.

